23
00:02:26,830 --> 00:02:28,330
When did you get back?

24
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:30,600
Last night.

25
00:02:32,510 --> 00:02:34,100
Everyone was out looking for you
last night.

26
00:02:34,640 --> 00:02:36,160
You're home. That's what matters.

27
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:37,780
Come on.

28
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:39,020
Let's eat.

29
00:02:39,210 --> 00:02:39,500
Come on.

30
00:02:50,660 --> 00:02:51,730
Eat some more, sweetheart.

31
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:52,920
Thanks.

32
00:02:53,730 --> 00:02:55,160
You didn't come home last night.

33
00:02:55,420 --> 00:02:56,290
Where have you been?

34
00:02:56,710 --> 00:02:57,660
Were you with Chita?

35
00:02:58,990 --> 00:03:00,500
Yeah. Last night, I...

36
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:07,190
Last night...

37
00:03:10,490 --> 00:03:11,680
I said goodbye to Chita.

38
00:03:16,640 --> 00:03:17,730
Did you get drunk and black out?

39
00:03:19,660 --> 00:03:20,120
Nin.

40
00:03:20,430 --> 00:03:21,910
Where does your brother drink?

41
00:03:22,910 --> 00:03:24,520
I won't mind if you have a drink
once in a while.

42
00:03:26,010 --> 00:03:27,060
- Okay.
- Eat up.

43
00:03:27,060 --> 00:03:28,530
Eat more. It'll make you stronger.

44
00:03:33,270 --> 00:03:33,760
Is it good?

45
00:03:47,170 --> 00:03:50,110
Oh, it just hit me.

46
00:03:50,110 --> 00:03:51,150
I have an unusual case.

47
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:52,510
A special emergency case.

48
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:53,970
Hurry and eat.

49
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,130
All right.

50
00:04:05,470 --> 00:04:06,220
You're feeling better, right?

51
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:10,900
I thought something happened to you.

52
00:04:12,270 --> 00:04:13,270
I'm right here.

53
00:04:13,890 --> 00:04:15,690
What could've happened?
You're acting weird.

54
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:19,640
Did the police catch Prae?

55
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:21,980
Prae?

56
00:04:24,070 --> 00:04:24,980
I just...

57
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:27,200
don't want to tell Mom about it.

58
00:04:28,460 --> 00:04:29,720
I'm afraid she'll get worse.

59
00:04:37,260 --> 00:04:38,300
You look out of it.

60
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:41,430
Why are you acting so strange today?

61
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:42,770
Uh...

62
00:04:53,510 --> 00:04:55,110
(Profile: Chidtawan)
Our target is Chidtawan.

63
00:04:55,110 --> 00:04:57,190
He's our only lead right now.

64
00:04:57,600 --> 00:05:01,030
He's 27, tall,
with a slim build.

65
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:03,050
He walks with a limp.

66
00:05:04,660 --> 00:05:05,970
The target isn't an ordinary human.

67
00:05:06,540 --> 00:05:08,740
I want every unit to deploy
all available personnel.

68
00:05:08,930 --> 00:05:10,280
If you spot him, don't hesitate.

69
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:11,750
Arrest him immediately,

70
00:05:11,880 --> 00:05:13,270
and report to me right away.

71
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:17,470
As for the killer being a Nour,

72
00:05:18,020 --> 00:05:19,520
keep it strictly confidential.

73
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:21,380
- Yes, Inspector.
- Yes.

74
00:05:22,070 --> 00:05:24,270
I've put every district on alert.

75
00:05:24,940 --> 00:05:27,160
Chidtawan knows
we've identified him,

76
00:05:27,700 --> 00:05:28,800
so he may try to flee.

77
00:05:31,140 --> 00:05:32,210
Based on what we know,

78
00:05:33,290 --> 00:05:34,760
a Nour can only feed on blood.

79
00:05:35,870 --> 00:05:36,440
Officer Phong.

80
00:05:37,210 --> 00:05:38,770
I want you to go to the hospital.

81
00:05:39,890 --> 00:05:41,010
He might go there to steal blood.

82
00:05:43,530 --> 00:05:44,930
We're in position.

83
00:05:46,140 --> 00:05:48,180
Tangme, go to Chita's dorm.

84
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:50,550
There's a good chance he'll return.

85
00:07:13,570 --> 00:07:14,000
Dr. Ji.

86
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:17,150
What are you doing?

87
00:07:24,770 --> 00:07:25,590
Where did you go?

88
00:07:31,770 --> 00:07:32,920
What happened that night?

89
00:07:35,110 --> 00:07:36,540
Tell me everything.

90
00:07:41,010 --> 00:07:42,150
I don't remember anything.

91
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:45,400
All I know is...

92
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:47,830
I was saying goodbye to Chita.

93
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:52,800
Then everything went blank.

94
00:07:56,250 --> 00:07:57,730
You're not hiding something

95
00:08:00,020 --> 00:08:01,050
to protect Chita, are you?

96
00:08:07,380 --> 00:08:08,290
Why would you say that?

97
00:08:10,220 --> 00:08:11,270
Why would I protect Chita?

98
00:08:16,110 --> 00:08:18,200
I'm asking why you'd say that.

99
00:08:23,310 --> 00:08:24,160
This is Prae's body.

100
00:08:25,950 --> 00:08:27,570
Chita burned her to death.

101
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:34,030
What I've searched for all my life

102
00:08:36,230 --> 00:08:38,530
was beside you all along, Dr. Ji.

103
00:08:40,990 --> 00:08:41,920
How can you be sure?

104
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:43,420
I saw it myself.

105
00:08:55,820 --> 00:08:56,820
I saw it myself.

106
00:08:56,820 --> 00:08:57,990
That's enough.

107
00:09:00,830 --> 00:09:01,540
Stop right there.

108
00:09:09,390 --> 00:09:10,720
I'll assume you didn't mean it.

109
00:09:14,470 --> 00:09:15,410
If you see him,

110
00:09:17,030 --> 00:09:18,340
tell me immediately.

111
00:09:19,710 --> 00:09:20,540
You know that, don't you, Doctor?

112
00:09:22,590 --> 00:09:25,480
I've spent my whole life searching
for the Nour that can kill Nour.

113
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:54,490
Dr. Ji looked shocked.

114
00:09:56,070 --> 00:09:57,200
I don't think he knew

115
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:59,030
Chita was behind all of this.

116
00:10:02,030 --> 00:10:04,080
Either way,
we need to keep watching Dr. Ji.

117
00:10:05,630 --> 00:10:07,320
Dr. Ji could be the wild card

118
00:10:08,310 --> 00:10:10,140
that leads us to Chita.

119
00:10:24,010 --> 00:10:25,890
I let you go in first on purpose.

120
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:28,520
I wanted to know

121
00:10:30,570 --> 00:10:31,960
what you'd say to Dr. Ji.

122
00:10:35,010 --> 00:10:36,610
And it went exactly as I expected.

123
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:46,210
All this time...

124
00:10:48,930 --> 00:10:49,910
I thought...

125
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:53,650
you were happy with me

126
00:10:57,060 --> 00:10:58,730
and wanted to spend your life with me.

127
00:11:04,130 --> 00:11:06,430
But now I'm not sure

128
00:11:07,870 --> 00:11:08,870
whether what I believed

129
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:11,720
was ever true.

130
00:11:21,730 --> 00:11:22,500
All this time...

131
00:11:26,030 --> 00:11:27,640
I really have been happy.

132
00:11:30,730 --> 00:11:31,500
Because of you.

133
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:41,250
The life you see now

134
00:11:44,980 --> 00:11:46,570
isn't my real life.

135
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:52,490
It was given to me by someone else.

136
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:58,990
And I have to give it back to him.

137
00:12:09,390 --> 00:12:11,100
There's a place I'd like to show you.

138
00:12:15,910 --> 00:12:17,460
Hey, after the exam tomorrow,

139
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:18,850
want to go grab a drink?

140
00:12:20,070 --> 00:12:21,290
All you think about is drinking.

141
00:12:21,630 --> 00:12:22,180
No.

142
00:12:22,270 --> 00:12:24,440
Come on. Music and dancing!

143
00:12:24,750 --> 00:12:26,180
No, I don't like it.

144
00:12:34,800 --> 00:12:35,800
It must be urgent.

145
00:12:36,150 --> 00:12:37,090
Go check upstairs.

146
00:12:37,410 --> 00:12:37,800
What?

147
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:28,800
Ji! What are you doing? Let go!

148
00:14:30,330 --> 00:14:30,950
Let go! Stop!

149
00:14:30,950 --> 00:14:31,350
Nin!

150
00:14:31,460 --> 00:14:31,910
Nin, let go!

151
00:14:44,970 --> 00:14:46,050
Ji, what's wrong? Let go!

152
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:48,450
Let go!

153
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:51,920
Let go!

154
00:14:52,730 --> 00:14:54,170
Ji, let go! What's wrong with you?

155
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:56,170
Nin!

156
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:57,420
Let go of my friend, you monster!

157
00:14:58,380 --> 00:14:58,800
Ow!

158
00:14:59,580 --> 00:15:00,560
Nin, go!

159
00:15:00,700 --> 00:15:02,310
Nin! Nin, get outside!

160
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:04,850
Hey! Let go!

161
00:15:05,290 --> 00:15:05,900
Nin!

162
00:15:06,450 --> 00:15:06,870
Let go!

163
00:15:07,080 --> 00:15:07,800
Nin!

164
00:15:07,850 --> 00:15:08,310
Get out!

165
00:15:08,730 --> 00:15:09,600
Let go of me!

166
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:10,010
Get out!

167
00:15:10,170 --> 00:15:11,150
Ji, let go!

168
00:15:11,220 --> 00:15:11,860
Get out!

169
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:15,670
What's wrong with you? Get out!

170
00:15:16,190 --> 00:15:17,800
I said get out!

171
00:15:20,900 --> 00:15:22,160
Go! Just go!

172
00:15:22,430 --> 00:15:24,090
- Go! Hurry!
- I'm sorry, Nin.

173
00:15:24,550 --> 00:15:25,340
Nin, I didn't mean it.

174
00:15:28,530 --> 00:15:29,060
Nin.

175
00:15:29,060 --> 00:15:30,030
Nin, I'm sorry.

176
00:15:30,530 --> 00:15:31,150
Nin, I'm sorry.

177
00:15:55,220 --> 00:15:57,150
Nin, I'm sorry.

178
00:15:57,960 --> 00:15:59,090
Nin, I'm sorry.

179
00:16:21,830 --> 00:16:22,750
(Dr. Ji, is that you?)

180
00:16:30,150 --> 00:16:31,460
My true love is buried here.

181
00:16:33,270 --> 00:16:33,980
True love?

182
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:37,460
I told you before, didn't I?

183
00:16:39,030 --> 00:16:40,380
About how to become a Nour.

184
00:16:41,130 --> 00:16:42,020
A Nour

185
00:16:43,180 --> 00:16:45,090
must bite through
their true love's heart.

186
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:50,110
But that isn't how I did it.

187
00:16:54,860 --> 00:16:56,190
All I could do...

188
00:16:58,510 --> 00:16:59,540
was to take his body

189
00:17:01,580 --> 00:17:03,540
and bury him here,
at the source of the Chao Phraya River.

190
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:12,790
A place we never had the chance

191
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:16,420
to visit while he was alive.

192
00:17:18,410 --> 00:17:19,540
For other Nour,

193
00:17:21,600 --> 00:17:22,800
becoming Nour

194
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:24,950
means staying with their true love

195
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,010
for eternity.

196
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:30,840
But for me...

197
00:17:32,350 --> 00:17:33,470
eternal life

198
00:17:34,670 --> 00:17:36,160
cost my true love his life.

199
00:17:42,530 --> 00:17:43,680
You might think

200
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:45,710
eternal life

201
00:17:46,590 --> 00:17:47,400
is a gift.

202
00:17:49,490 --> 00:17:50,310
It isn't.

203
00:17:54,470 --> 00:17:55,540
In my life,

204
00:17:57,090 --> 00:17:58,160
I can't eat.

205
00:17:59,670 --> 00:18:00,710
I can't sleep.

206
00:18:02,260 --> 00:18:03,800
I can't even die when I want to.

207
00:18:06,370 --> 00:18:08,390
It feels more like a curse.

208
00:18:13,490 --> 00:18:15,090
The longer I live,

209
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:18,430
I have to keep changing my name

210
00:18:19,470 --> 00:18:20,710
and taking on new identities,

211
00:18:22,900 --> 00:18:23,800
until sometimes...

212
00:18:25,320 --> 00:18:27,470
I even forget my own past.

213
00:18:31,260 --> 00:18:32,410
I forget who I am.

214
00:18:35,690 --> 00:18:36,490
And I forget...

215
00:18:38,190 --> 00:18:40,600
why I'm still living at all.

216
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:45,900
All I can do is accept my fate,

217
00:18:47,410 --> 00:18:49,620
surviving on other people's blood,

218
00:18:51,110 --> 00:18:52,240
using someone else's name,

219
00:18:53,970 --> 00:18:55,180
living in someone else's home.

220
00:18:58,430 --> 00:19:00,970
Nothing in my life
truly belongs to me.

221
00:19:08,920 --> 00:19:11,020
Do you understand what I want now?

222
00:19:14,390 --> 00:19:14,790
No.

223
00:19:16,500 --> 00:19:17,520
I never will.

224
00:19:19,390 --> 00:19:20,580
You think dying

225
00:19:21,310 --> 00:19:23,260
will repay the life
you owe your true love?

226
00:19:27,530 --> 00:19:28,620
I'll make sure

227
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:31,140
you see that living well

228
00:19:32,270 --> 00:19:33,400
is how you'll find peace

229
00:19:33,980 --> 00:19:36,250
and break free from the curse
and everything haunting you.

230
00:19:59,760 --> 00:20:00,660
Let me check the wound.

231
00:20:03,870 --> 00:20:04,490
Whoa.

232
00:20:05,340 --> 00:20:06,450
It's bleeding through.

233
00:20:07,070 --> 00:20:07,920
Want a new bandage?

234
00:20:08,570 --> 00:20:09,120
I'm fine.

235
00:20:12,750 --> 00:20:13,810
Fine. Suit yourself.

236
00:20:17,500 --> 00:20:17,970
By the way,

237
00:20:19,030 --> 00:20:19,950
where's your mom?

238
00:20:21,660 --> 00:20:23,140
She went upstairs to sleep.

239
00:20:25,860 --> 00:20:27,280
Luckily, she was out earlier.

240
00:20:28,270 --> 00:20:30,960
When she came back, I lied and said
my brother had an emergency.

241
00:20:31,420 --> 00:20:32,230
You lied to your mom?

242
00:20:34,680 --> 00:20:35,370
Yeah.

243
00:20:40,430 --> 00:20:41,290
Let me ask you something.

244
00:20:43,390 --> 00:20:44,810
What will you do about your brother?

245
00:20:51,150 --> 00:20:51,670
Honestly...

246
00:20:54,220 --> 00:20:54,800
right now...

247
00:20:57,500 --> 00:20:58,320
I'm terrified.

248
00:21:02,260 --> 00:21:02,920
You saw him.

249
00:21:04,310 --> 00:21:05,830
You saw what he was like.

250
00:21:07,360 --> 00:21:08,510
But what scares me more

251
00:21:10,130 --> 00:21:10,700
is that...

252
00:21:13,260 --> 00:21:14,480
I'll never be able to see him
the same way again.

253
00:21:17,800 --> 00:21:20,680
If my brother starts killing people

254
00:21:21,640 --> 00:21:23,170
or drinking people's blood...

255
00:21:26,990 --> 00:21:28,280
how can I still see him as my brother?

256
00:21:29,390 --> 00:21:30,280
And then there's Mom.

257
00:21:31,950 --> 00:21:33,040
She'd never be able to handle it.

258
00:21:35,050 --> 00:21:37,980
My brother means everything to her.

259
00:21:41,680 --> 00:21:42,810
Just answer one question.

260
00:21:44,710 --> 00:21:45,690
Do you still love your brother?

261
00:21:47,070 --> 00:21:47,450
Of course.

262
00:21:49,170 --> 00:21:49,820
Exactly.

263
00:21:51,880 --> 00:21:53,720
Love is stupid like that.

264
00:21:54,180 --> 00:21:55,740
Even after what he's done,

265
00:21:56,350 --> 00:21:57,350
you still love him.

266
00:21:58,360 --> 00:22:01,540
Love and reason
will always be at odds.

267
00:22:02,410 --> 00:22:04,620
You saw how hard he tried, right?

268
00:22:05,600 --> 00:22:07,180
He fought hard to keep himself

269
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:09,130
from biting you.

270
00:22:11,140 --> 00:22:11,680
Exactly.

271
00:22:12,280 --> 00:22:13,500
That alone proves

272
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:14,820
he's still trying.

273
00:22:16,020 --> 00:22:17,020
And that same faith,

274
00:22:17,990 --> 00:22:19,630
I hope you can hold on to it too.

275
00:22:20,790 --> 00:22:22,720
You have to believe
he can become himself again.

276
00:22:25,950 --> 00:22:26,960
But don't put too much pressure
on yourself.

277
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:31,060
No matter what happens next,

278
00:22:32,830 --> 00:22:34,190
the person who'll stay by your side

279
00:22:34,890 --> 00:22:35,430
will be me.

280
00:22:38,120 --> 00:22:39,110
You can count on that.

281
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:40,420
Yeah.

282
00:22:41,010 --> 00:22:42,080
I promise.

283
00:22:44,360 --> 00:22:45,030
Thanks, man.

284
00:22:47,490 --> 00:22:48,240
Let's deal with that wound.

285
00:22:50,320 --> 00:22:52,160
No bandages, though.
Want me to spit on it?

286
00:22:53,380 --> 00:22:54,280
Not the time for jokes.

287
00:23:01,190 --> 00:23:02,990
Phong sent people
to Chita's dorm.

288
00:23:03,110 --> 00:23:04,430
Dr. Jirat came here looking for him.

289
00:23:19,420 --> 00:23:20,380
What did you do to me, Chita?

290
00:23:21,280 --> 00:23:21,640
Doctor.

291
00:23:24,420 --> 00:23:25,390
- Dr. Ji.
- What did you do to me?

292
00:23:36,480 --> 00:23:37,860
Tell me. What did you do to me?

293
00:23:37,860 --> 00:23:38,620
Doctor, listen to me.

294
00:23:40,820 --> 00:23:41,530
Doctor.

295
00:23:42,870 --> 00:23:44,050
We can't stay here, Doctor.

296
00:23:46,070 --> 00:23:46,900
We have to leave.

297
00:23:49,900 --> 00:23:50,830
I'm not going anywhere.

298
00:23:52,430 --> 00:23:54,020
First tell me what happened.

299
00:24:01,500 --> 00:24:02,610
Calm down.

300
00:24:04,190 --> 00:24:05,540
We have to leave, Doctor.

301
00:24:15,640 --> 00:24:16,220
Chita.

302
00:24:18,240 --> 00:24:19,040
Do you know...

303
00:24:21,190 --> 00:24:22,930
I almost killed my brother today?

304
00:24:38,880 --> 00:24:39,660
Tell me the truth.

305
00:24:42,800 --> 00:24:44,130
You were already dead back then.

306
00:24:51,090 --> 00:24:52,230
See you tomorrow, Chita.

307
00:24:53,230 --> 00:24:53,790
See you tomorrow.

308
00:24:55,640 --> 00:24:57,280
When we said goodbye that day,

309
00:24:59,930 --> 00:25:01,880
Prae must've been chased here.

310
00:25:02,680 --> 00:25:03,620
She was injured.

311
00:25:04,310 --> 00:25:05,770
And she happened to run into you.

312
00:25:22,200 --> 00:25:23,800
I was just a step too late.

313
00:25:24,200 --> 00:25:26,680
It's all my fault.

314
00:25:27,400 --> 00:25:28,680
I didn't get here in time to save you.

315
00:25:59,160 --> 00:25:59,600
Doctor.

316
00:27:24,240 --> 00:27:24,680
Doctor.

317
00:27:40,730 --> 00:27:41,840
No.

318
00:27:42,620 --> 00:27:42,980
Doctor.

319
00:27:47,220 --> 00:27:48,640
I don't want to lose you.

320
00:27:49,220 --> 00:27:50,680
I had no choice.

321
00:27:53,170 --> 00:27:54,950
So I decided to change you.

322
00:28:36,660 --> 00:28:38,460
Doctor.

323
00:28:42,030 --> 00:28:43,290
Wake up!

324
00:29:03,420 --> 00:29:04,950
But you still didn't wake up.

325
00:29:06,550 --> 00:29:08,130
At first, I thought it hadn't worked.

326
00:29:09,930 --> 00:29:12,480
I was afraid we weren't
each other's true love.

327
00:29:13,060 --> 00:29:14,730
Doctor, wake up!

328
00:31:06,130 --> 00:31:06,580
Chita.

329
00:31:08,590 --> 00:31:09,000
Chita.

330
00:31:35,400 --> 00:31:36,170
But look.

331
00:31:37,590 --> 00:31:38,490
You're with me now.

332
00:31:42,070 --> 00:31:43,820
Because we're each other's true love.

333
00:31:49,010 --> 00:31:49,590
Chita.

334
00:31:51,700 --> 00:31:52,990
So you killed all those people.

335
00:31:54,060 --> 00:31:55,020
You killed Somying.

336
00:31:55,760 --> 00:31:56,500
You killed Tee.

337
00:31:57,400 --> 00:31:58,200
You killed Prae.

338
00:31:59,860 --> 00:32:00,470
Didn't you?

339
00:32:06,740 --> 00:32:07,440
They were all Nour.

340
00:32:11,710 --> 00:32:12,880
They deserved to die, Doctor.

341
00:32:17,300 --> 00:32:18,410
Then kill me too.

342
00:32:20,670 --> 00:32:21,570
I'm Nour too.

343
00:32:27,590 --> 00:32:28,630
You're different.

344
00:32:31,350 --> 00:32:32,130
You know...

345
00:32:32,780 --> 00:32:34,030
I'd never hurt you.

346
00:32:40,310 --> 00:32:41,260
Doctor.

347
00:32:42,690 --> 00:32:43,420
Come with me.

348
00:32:46,070 --> 00:32:46,400
No.

349
00:32:48,550 --> 00:32:49,120
Please, Doctor.

350
00:32:52,220 --> 00:32:52,670
Doctor.

351
00:32:53,840 --> 00:32:54,450
Let me go.

352
00:32:55,240 --> 00:32:55,800
Let me go!

353
00:32:55,860 --> 00:32:57,130
Doctor! Listen to me!

354
00:32:58,920 --> 00:32:59,440
Doctor.

355
00:33:00,300 --> 00:33:00,580
Let go!

356
00:33:00,700 --> 00:33:01,550
Doctor! Doctor!

357
00:33:05,820 --> 00:33:06,890
Doctor, don't go!

358
00:33:06,890 --> 00:33:08,150
Please listen to me.

359
00:33:08,400 --> 00:33:08,890
Doctor.

360
00:33:22,130 --> 00:33:22,540
Doctor.

361
00:33:25,220 --> 00:33:26,140
Doctor! Doctor!

362
00:33:33,600 --> 00:33:34,730
Doctor!

363
00:33:56,710 --> 00:33:57,490
Where is everyone?

364
00:33:58,200 --> 00:33:59,160
(People's Police Station)
Tangme's car is gone too.

365
00:34:00,280 --> 00:34:02,380
(People's Police Station)
Wait here. I'll go upstairs for my gun.

366
00:34:22,700 --> 00:34:24,300
(Can anyone hear me?
Can anyone hear me?)

367
00:34:25,530 --> 00:34:26,180
What's wrong, Officer Phong?

368
00:34:26,480 --> 00:34:27,240
James, where are you?

369
00:34:27,430 --> 00:34:28,280
Tangme already went inside.

370
00:34:28,470 --> 00:34:29,410
(Repeat, Tangme is already inside.)

371
00:34:29,840 --> 00:34:31,010
Tell Tangme not to go in.

372
00:34:31,540 --> 00:34:32,530
I'm on my way.

373
00:34:42,650 --> 00:34:44,690
(People's Police Station)

374
00:36:00,400 --> 00:36:01,000
Dr. Jirat.

375
00:36:06,420 --> 00:36:07,150
Dr. Jirat.

376
00:36:08,550 --> 00:36:09,400
Are you okay?

377
00:36:11,800 --> 00:36:12,710
Doctor, can you hear me?

378
00:36:14,220 --> 00:36:14,980
Doctor, what's wrong?

379
00:36:17,820 --> 00:36:18,320
Doctor.

380
00:36:18,420 --> 00:36:19,550
Stay with me, Doctor.

381
00:36:19,550 --> 00:36:20,430
Doctor.

382
00:36:20,430 --> 00:36:21,690
Dr. Ji! Doctor!

383
00:36:21,840 --> 00:36:22,650
Doctor.

384
00:36:42,820 --> 00:36:44,000
Don't shoot him.

385
00:36:45,640 --> 00:36:47,000
He's not complete yet.

386
00:36:48,660 --> 00:36:50,020
He could die.

387
00:36:50,880 --> 00:36:51,700
Sorry about this.

388
00:40:23,930 --> 00:40:24,750
Doctor.

389
00:40:30,440 --> 00:40:31,450
Let's live together.

390
00:40:33,780 --> 00:40:35,320
You wanted to go abroad, right?

391
00:40:38,990 --> 00:40:39,880
Let's go together.

392
00:40:54,800 --> 00:40:55,510
Doctor.

393
00:40:57,000 --> 00:40:57,820
How can I?

394
00:41:00,970 --> 00:41:01,970
What about my family?

395
00:41:05,150 --> 00:41:06,270
Like I told you,

396
00:41:07,460 --> 00:41:08,640
once you've adjusted,

397
00:41:10,260 --> 00:41:11,160
we'll come back.

398
00:41:12,990 --> 00:41:14,820
When everything settles down,

399
00:41:17,340 --> 00:41:19,310
I'll find a way
to help you adjust to this life.

400
00:41:21,830 --> 00:41:23,480
You don't have to be afraid
when you're with me.

401
00:41:33,890 --> 00:41:36,240
Why are you looking at me like that?

402
00:41:38,150 --> 00:41:38,650
Doctor.

403
00:41:40,220 --> 00:41:40,950
I'm scared.

404
00:41:45,640 --> 00:41:46,400
Of what?

405
00:41:49,000 --> 00:41:49,680
I'm scared.

406
00:41:52,480 --> 00:41:53,290
What are you scared of?

407
00:41:53,300 --> 00:41:54,350
I'm really scared of you.

408
00:41:59,730 --> 00:42:00,660
Why would you say that?

409
00:42:02,540 --> 00:42:03,850
I'm scared of myself too.

410
00:42:07,070 --> 00:42:08,130
I hate myself.

411
00:42:09,990 --> 00:42:10,770
No, no, no.

412
00:42:11,950 --> 00:42:13,890
Don't be afraid.
You're with me now.

413
00:42:15,970 --> 00:42:17,160
Look at what you've done.

414
00:42:22,160 --> 00:42:23,220
Just look.

415
00:42:26,340 --> 00:42:27,530
You think you're helping me?

416
00:42:28,840 --> 00:42:29,550
I was only trying...

417
00:42:29,880 --> 00:42:31,270
I really was trying to help you.

418
00:42:33,550 --> 00:42:34,420
But you killed me.

419
00:42:35,440 --> 00:42:36,810
Do you understand?
You killed me.

420
00:42:38,580 --> 00:42:39,220
Chita.

421
00:42:42,640 --> 00:42:43,210
I...

422
00:42:45,880 --> 00:42:46,740
gave everything I had

423
00:42:50,240 --> 00:42:51,060
to become a doctor,

424
00:42:52,520 --> 00:42:53,550
to save lives.

425
00:42:56,730 --> 00:42:58,500
If I become a killer like you,

426
00:43:01,050 --> 00:43:03,000
I'd rather be dead.

427
00:43:05,030 --> 00:43:05,450
Why?

428
00:43:08,960 --> 00:43:09,950
Why would you say that?

429
00:43:12,110 --> 00:43:13,100
I want to die.

430
00:43:15,700 --> 00:43:18,560
You can't die.
You must stay with me.

431
00:43:19,280 --> 00:43:21,050
You can't die!

432
00:43:22,620 --> 00:43:23,190
Doctor.

433
00:43:52,930 --> 00:43:53,430
Doctor.

434
00:43:54,930 --> 00:43:56,320
Doctor! Doctor!

435
00:43:56,850 --> 00:43:58,150
Doctor, what happened?

436
00:44:01,140 --> 00:44:01,700
Doctor.

437
00:44:04,820 --> 00:44:05,830
Have you seen Tangme?

438
00:44:07,050 --> 00:44:07,940
The female officer.

439
00:44:09,000 --> 00:44:10,830
The one who works
with Inspector Ken and me.

440
00:44:13,680 --> 00:44:14,560
Have you seen her?

441
00:44:16,670 --> 00:44:17,530
Tangme?

442
00:44:18,130 --> 00:44:18,720
Tangme?

443
00:44:19,480 --> 00:44:19,880
Tangme?

444
00:44:20,810 --> 00:44:21,380
Tangme?

445
00:44:24,270 --> 00:44:25,050
Doctor, what happened?

446
00:44:27,290 --> 00:44:27,760
Tangme?

447
00:44:28,680 --> 00:44:29,230
Tangme?

448
00:44:29,240 --> 00:44:30,150
What's all this blood?

449
00:44:31,110 --> 00:44:31,760
Tangme?

450
00:44:34,490 --> 00:44:35,140
I didn't do it.

451
00:44:35,800 --> 00:44:36,670
- What did you do?
- I...

452
00:44:36,670 --> 00:44:37,170
I didn't do it.

453
00:44:37,800 --> 00:44:38,280
It wasn't me.

454
00:44:39,140 --> 00:44:39,790
What did you do?

455
00:44:40,320 --> 00:44:41,000
It wasn't me.

456
00:44:41,420 --> 00:44:42,040
I didn't do it.

457
00:44:42,660 --> 00:44:44,050
What do you mean, it wasn't you?
Answer me!

458
00:44:52,550 --> 00:44:53,140
Tangme.

459
00:44:53,560 --> 00:44:53,960
Tangme.

460
00:44:54,110 --> 00:44:55,540
Hey, Tangme!

461
00:44:55,540 --> 00:44:56,950
Get up!

462
00:44:57,880 --> 00:44:59,470
Someone help us!

463
00:44:59,990 --> 00:45:01,590
Hey! We need help!

464
00:45:05,610 --> 00:45:07,460
(Tangme! Tangme!)

465
00:45:07,460 --> 00:45:08,970
(Tangme, no!)

466
00:45:10,790 --> 00:45:11,510
Tangme is dead.

467
00:45:13,050 --> 00:45:13,840
Tangme is dead.

468
00:45:17,770 --> 00:45:20,130
(James, where are you?
Come help me!)

469
00:45:21,150 --> 00:45:23,330
(James, where are you?)

470
00:45:23,330 --> 00:45:25,330
(Tangme!)

471
00:45:46,880 --> 00:45:48,120
Chita did this, didn't he?

472
00:45:49,630 --> 00:45:51,230
That Chita guy did this, didn't he?

473
00:45:52,360 --> 00:45:53,450
Or was it you, Doctor?

474
00:45:55,910 --> 00:45:57,360
I need to know who to stab.

475
00:46:02,930 --> 00:46:03,620
Doctor, run!

476
00:46:03,710 --> 00:46:04,080
Chita!

477
00:46:04,540 --> 00:46:05,260
- Doctor, run!
- Chita!

478
00:46:05,510 --> 00:46:05,900
Chita!

479
00:46:06,830 --> 00:46:07,140
Chita!

480
00:46:24,180 --> 00:46:25,230
You did it, didn't you?

481
00:46:26,500 --> 00:46:27,360
She shouldn't have come in.

482
00:46:29,690 --> 00:46:30,600
This isn't what I wanted.

483
00:46:45,780 --> 00:46:46,630
This one's for Tangme.

484
00:47:15,240 --> 00:47:15,970
And this one...

485
00:47:16,640 --> 00:47:17,800
is for my dad.

486
00:47:30,420 --> 00:47:31,020
Doctor.

487
00:47:32,040 --> 00:47:33,020
I'm sorry.

488
00:48:05,940 --> 00:48:10,570
♪In a love that can never be real♪

489
00:48:12,840 --> 00:48:17,670
♪You gaze in my soul
and share what I feel♪

490
00:48:20,040 --> 00:48:24,800
♪Gray days all fade away, I'm healed♪

491
00:48:26,750 --> 00:48:31,930
♪My dull world starts to glow and shine♪

492
00:48:34,110 --> 00:48:40,440
♪Bound by fate we cannot break
Silent thoughts we both share♪

493
00:48:41,190 --> 00:48:47,050
♪Found a light no dark can shake♪

494
00:48:47,840 --> 00:48:53,490
♪We make a wish toward rainbow's end♪

495
00:48:55,210 --> 00:49:00,520
♪Chase the dream beyond the bend♪

496
00:49:02,330 --> 00:49:08,930
♪Though this hope
can never reach the ground♪

497
00:49:09,070 --> 00:49:14,390
♪You painted hues in my barren land♪

498
00:49:18,190 --> 00:49:24,800
♪In lonely nights I used to fall
Till your eyes broke through my shell♪

499
00:49:25,280 --> 00:49:32,070
♪Hidden love we dare not tell
Sweet moments time can't quell♪

500
00:49:34,130 --> 00:49:40,690
♪Bound by fate we cannot break
Silent thoughts we both share♪

501
00:49:41,150 --> 00:49:47,160
♪Found a light no dark can shake♪

